      aboutTitle: 'About Us',
      conceptTitle: 'THE CONCEPT',
      conceptContent: 'EducAmbiental is a pioneering mobile application, developed by Mexican talent, with the mission of transforming the way we manage our urban waste. Born from the desire to protect our environment and promote ecological education, the platform helps society correctly separate their waste from home through an interactive system.\n\nWith EducAmbiental, your good deeds count. We connect citizens with local Recycling Centers through geolocation technology, making it easier for your waste to reach the right place. Learning to recycle has never been so easy.',
      savingPlanetTitle: 'SAVING OUR PLANET',
      savingPlanetContent: 'True change starts at home. Correctly separating your waste drastically increases the recovery rate of recyclable materials and decreases the amount of trash that ends up in landfills. This translates into a firect reduction of carbon dioxide and greenhouse gas emissions.\n\nBy using our Interactive Catalog to learn how to clean and classify plastics, glass, cardboard, and organics, you are ensuring that those materials can be reincorporated into the circular economy. Manufacturing new products from recycled materials requires significantly less energy and avoids the devastation caused by the extraction of virgin raw materials. Your active participation gives the Earth a breather.',
      wasteRealityTitle: 'THE REALITY OF WASTE',
      wasteRealityContent: 'A landfill is not a simple trash dump; it is a facility designed to bury municipal solid waste. When organic matter (such as food scraps or wet paper) is buried and decomposes without oxygen, anaerobic digestion occurs. This biological process generates large amounts of methane, a greenhouse gas much more potent and destructive than carbon dioxide.\n\nMinimizing the release of these gases is vital to slowing global warming. By diverting recyclable materials from these landfills and taking them to Recycling Centers through our network, you are directly fighting climate change.\n\nKnowledge is power, but action is what transforms the world. Change only happens when individuals take the initiative. Join the EducAmbiental community and make your impact count!',
